.SH NAME
niac-template-show - Show template contents


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBniac template show  [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Print the YAML body of a named template to stdout. Useful for
inspecting what a template will produce or piping it into another tool
without writing to disk.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for show


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--storage-keep\fP=500
	Run history records to keep, pruned oldest first on start (0 keeps every run)

.PP
\fB--storage-path\fP=""
	Path to NIAC run history database (default: ~/.niac/niac.db)


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  # Show basic network template
  niac template show basic-network

  # Show small office template
  niac template show small-office

  # Pipe to file
  niac template show data-center > my-config.yaml
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBniac-template(1)\fP


